Given a scheme $T$ over $S$ we can consider morphisms
$b : T \times_S Z \to T \times_S X$ over $S$. Picture
\begin{equation}
\vcenter{
\xymatrix{
T \times_S Z \ar[rd] \ar[rr]_b & &
T \times_S X \ar[ld] & Z \ar[rd] & & X \ar[ld] \\
& T \ar[rrr] & & & S
}
}
